IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`

-- je21-art01-definitions: Article 1 (Interpretation) of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 (L.8/2021).
--
-- Article 1 opens "In this Law, unless the context indicates otherwise –".
-- Whether the context indicates otherwise is a judgement about the passage in which a word is used, so every function here takes it as an input
-- (`the context indicates otherwise`) and refuses when it is TRUE: the Law does not say what the context would supply instead.
--
-- The definitions that only point at another Article ("as-enacted legislation", "consolidated legislation", "made", "official version"), and the ones that name an office
-- or a body with nothing a reader could ask about it ("current drafting practice", "Legislative Drafting Office", "Principal Legislative Drafter", "standing orders", "UK Act"),
-- are in the coverage table of NOTES.md as `inert`, each with its reason.
-- "Legislative Drafter" is here because Article 22 turns on it.

§ `Article 1 -- Interpretation`

§§ `"Law", "Jersey subordinate legislation", "Jersey legislation", "UK extended legislation", "legislation"`

-- The definitions of "Law" and "Jersey legislation" are circular as printed:
-- a Law is "Jersey legislation adopted by the States that does not rely on any other legislation to empower its making", and "Jersey legislation" is "any Law or Jersey subordinate legislation".
-- Subordinate legislation is made under other legislation, so it relies on it, and what is left of the first definition is an instrument adopted by the States that relies on nothing else.
-- That is what this function tests.
-- src:15 | “Law” means Jersey legislation adopted by the States that does not rely on any other legislation to empower its making;
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 1 "Law" (src:15)
GIVEN instrument IS A `Facts about an instrument`
      `the context indicates otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 1 "Law": the instrument is a Law` instrument `the context indicates otherwise` MEANS
    IF `the context indicates otherwise`
    THEN REFUSE "Article 1 gives its definitions unless the context indicates otherwise, and the Law does not say what the context supplies instead"
    ELSE     instrument's `it was adopted by the States`
         AND NOT instrument's `it relies on other legislation to empower its making`

-- src:12 | “Jersey subordinate legislation” means any Regulations, Order or other instrument having legislative effect in Jersey that is made in Jersey under –
-- src:13 | (a) any Jersey legislation; or
-- src:14 | (b) any UK extended legislation or Order in Council registered in the Royal Court;
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 1 "Jersey subordinate legislation" (src:12-14)
GIVEN instrument IS A `Facts about an instrument`
      `the context indicates otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 1 "Jersey subordinate legislation": the instrument is Jersey subordinate legislation` instrument `the context indicates otherwise` MEANS
    IF `the context indicates otherwise`
    THEN REFUSE "Article 1 gives its definitions unless the context indicates otherwise, and the Law does not say what the context supplies instead"
    ELSE     instrument's `it is Regulations, an Order or another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey`
         AND instrument's `it was made in Jersey`
         AND CONSIDER instrument's `it is made under`
             WHEN `Jersey legislation` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `UK extended legislation or an Order in Council registered in the Royal Court` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `neither of these` THEN FALSE

-- src:11 | “Jersey legislation” means any Law or Jersey subordinate legislation;
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 1 "Jersey legislation" (src:11)
GIVEN instrument IS A `Facts about an instrument`
      `the context indicates otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 1 "Jersey legislation": the instrument is Jersey legislation` instrument `the context indicates otherwise` MEANS
        `Article 1 "Law": the instrument is a Law` instrument `the context indicates otherwise`
    OR  `Article 1 "Jersey subordinate legislation": the instrument is Jersey subordinate legislation` instrument `the context indicates otherwise`

-- src:27 | “UK Act” means any Act of the Parliament of the United Kingdom (irrespective of whether it applies to the whole of the United Kingdom);
-- src:28 | “UK extended legislation” means any provision of a UK Act, or subordinate legislation made under a UK Act, that has been registered in the Royal Court.[1]
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 1 "UK Act" and "UK extended legislation" (src:27-28)
GIVEN instrument IS A `Facts about an instrument`
      `the context indicates otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 1 "UK extended legislation": the instrument is UK extended legislation` instrument `the context indicates otherwise` MEANS
    IF `the context indicates otherwise`
    THEN REFUSE "Article 1 gives its definitions unless the context indicates otherwise, and the Law does not say what the context supplies instead"
    ELSE     instrument's `it is a provision of a UK Act, or subordinate legislation made under a UK Act`
         AND instrument's `it has been registered in the Royal Court`

-- src:16 | “legislation” means Jersey legislation and UK extended legislation;
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 1 "legislation" (src:16)
GIVEN instrument IS A `Facts about an instrument`
      `the context indicates otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 1 "legislation": the instrument is legislation` instrument `the context indicates otherwise` MEANS
        `Article 1 "Jersey legislation": the instrument is Jersey legislation` instrument `the context indicates otherwise`
    OR  `Article 1 "UK extended legislation": the instrument is UK extended legislation` instrument `the context indicates otherwise`

§§ `"triennial Regulations", "repeal", "revised", "publish", "Legislative Drafter"`

-- "triennial Regulations" is spelled with a small t here and a capital T in Article 2(3)(a) ("Triennial Regulations"); this module takes them to be the same thing.
-- src:26 | “triennial Regulations” means Regulations made under either or both of the Orders in Council dated 28th March 1771 and 14th April 1884;
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 1 "triennial Regulations" (src:26)
GIVEN `the instrument is Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they were made under the Order in Council dated 28th March 1771` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they were made under the Order in Council dated 14th April 1884` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context indicates otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 1 "triennial Regulations": the Regulations are triennial Regulations` `the instrument is Regulations` `they were made under the Order in Council dated 28th March 1771` `they were made under the Order in Council dated 14th April 1884` `the context indicates otherwise` MEANS
    IF `the context indicates otherwise`
    THEN REFUSE "Article 1 gives its definitions unless the context indicates otherwise, and the Law does not say what the context supplies instead"
    ELSE     `the instrument is Regulations`
         AND (   `they were made under the Order in Council dated 28th March 1771`
              OR `they were made under the Order in Council dated 14th April 1884`)

-- "includes" leaves the list open: a word the definition does not name is neither in nor out.
-- src:23 | “repeal” includes delete, rescind and revoke;
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 1 "repeal" (src:23)
GIVEN word IS A `Word used for ending legislation`
      `the context indicates otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 1 "repeal": what the Law does is a repeal` word `the context indicates otherwise` MEANS
    IF `the context indicates otherwise`
    THEN REFUSE "Article 1 gives its definitions unless the context indicates otherwise, and the Law does not say what the context supplies instead"
    ELSE CONSIDER word
         WHEN `the word repeal` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the word delete` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the word rescind` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the word revoke` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `another word` THEN REFUSE "Article 1 says only that repeal includes delete, rescind and revoke, and does not say whether any other word is a repeal"

-- src:24 | “revised”, in relation to Jersey legislation, means any legislation certified as such in accordance with Article 15(7);
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 1 "revised" (src:24)
GIVEN `the legislation has been certified as revised in accordance with Article 15(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context indicates otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 1 "revised": the legislation is revised` `the legislation has been certified as revised in accordance with Article 15(7)` `the context indicates otherwise` MEANS
    IF `the context indicates otherwise`
    THEN REFUSE "Article 1 gives its definitions unless the context indicates otherwise, and the Law does not say what the context supplies instead"
    ELSE `the legislation has been certified as revised in accordance with Article 15(7)`

-- "publish" has three limbs, all of which have to hold: made available, on an on-going basis, on a website that gives access free of charge.
-- src:22 | “publish”, in relation to legislation, means to make available, on an on-going basis, on a website that provides access to the legislation free of charge;
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 1 "publish" (src:22)
GIVEN `it is made available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made available on an on-going basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is on a website that provides access to the legislation free of charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context indicates otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 1 "publish": the legislation is published` `it is made available` `it is made available on an on-going basis` `it is on a website that provides access to the legislation free of charge` `the context indicates otherwise` MEANS
    IF `the context indicates otherwise`
    THEN REFUSE "Article 1 gives its definitions unless the context indicates otherwise, and the Law does not say what the context supplies instead"
    ELSE     `it is made available`
         AND `it is made available on an on-going basis`
         AND `it is on a website that provides access to the legislation free of charge`

-- src:17 | “Legislative Drafter” means any person employed (including under a contract for services) to draft legislation for the Legislative Drafting Office, and includes the Principal Legislative Drafter and any trainee Legislative Drafter;
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 1 "Legislative Drafter" (src:17)
GIVEN role IS A `Role in the Legislative Drafting Office`
      `the context indicates otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 1 "Legislative Drafter": the person is a Legislative Drafter` role `the context indicates otherwise` MEANS
    IF `the context indicates otherwise`
    THEN REFUSE "Article 1 gives its definitions unless the context indicates otherwise, and the Law does not say what the context supplies instead"
    ELSE CONSIDER role
         WHEN `employed, including under a contract for services, to draft legislation for the Legislative Drafting Office` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the Principal Legislative Drafter` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a trainee Legislative Drafter` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
